public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.KoszulGlobalHomCochain

/-!
# `RΓ(𝒞, K)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)` at an ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global sections

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `A` be a commutative ring with `ρ : A ⟶ Γ(𝒞, 𝒪)`, let
`a_1, …, a_r ∈ A` and let `ℐ = (ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r)𝒪` be the ideal sheaf they generate. This file
proves the identity of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX],

`RΓ(𝒞, K)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)`   in `D(A)`,

for an arbitrary object `K` of `D(𝒪)`: the derived completion on the left is taken along
`Ideal.span {a_1, …, a_r}` and is `DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor`, the reflector of
[Stacks, Tag 0G3E]; the derived completion on the right is taken along `ℐ` and is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion`, the reflector of [Stacks, Tag 099F], which
exists at such an `ℐ` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`. There is
no nilpotence, boundedness or finiteness hypothesis, and neither reflector is carried as an
`IsRightAdjoint` hypothesis.

## The argument

Both sides are derived limits of the *same* tower, and the whole content is the identification
of the two towers.

1. *The sheaf side.*
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedGlobalSections_derivedSheafHomSystem` of
   `GlobalSectionsKoszulDerivedLimit.lean`: `RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)` is a derived limit of
   `n ↦ RΓ_A(𝒞, R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K^n, K))`, where `K^n = K(𝒪, f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})`.
2. *The passage to complexes.* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedKoszulHomTowerComparison` of
   `KoszulGlobalHomCochain.lean`: for a K-injective representative `J` of `K` that tower is the
   image in `D(A)` of the complex-level tower `n ↦ Γ_A(𝒞, SheafHom•_𝒪(K^n, J))`.
3. *The identification of the two complex-level towers.*
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionsKoszulSheafHomComplexSystemIso` of the same file:
   that tower is `KoszulCoefficientTower.coefficientKoszulTower a` applied to `Γ_A(𝒞, J)`.
4. *The module side.* `KoszulCompletion.isDerivedLimit_coefficientKoszulTower_derivedCompletion`
   of `KoszulCoefficientDerivedCompletion.lean`: the derived completion of `Γ_A(𝒞, J)` is a
   derived limit of that tower.
5. `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.nonempty_iso_of_isDerivedLimit` identifies the two derived
   limits, and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_moduleGlobalSectionsDerivedUnit_app` rewrites
   `Q(Γ_A(𝒞, J))` as `RΓ_A(𝒞, K)`, `J` being K-injective.

The isomorphism is a `Nonempty`, not a construction, for the reason recorded with
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.nonempty_iso_of_isDerivedLimit`: a derived limit is determined
only up to non-unique isomorphism, which is why `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit`
is a predicate.

## Main results

* `RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections_of_isKInjective`: the
  identity for a K-injective complex `J`, which is the form the argument produces.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections`: **the
  identity for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`.** Every object of `D(𝒪)` is the class of a complex,
  `CategoryTheory.Functor.EssSurj` for `DerivedCategory.Q`, and every complex has a K-injective
  resolution, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveResolution`, so the K-injective case
  suffices.

## Why there is no `@[stacks 0BLX]` attribute here

[Stacks, Tag 0BLX] asserts the identity **and two spectral sequences**, and a tag's attribute
goes only on a declaration stating the whole tag. The two spectral sequences are registered
separately —
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_spectralSequence_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletion.lean` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_generatedIdealSheaf`
of `GlobalSectionsCompletionGenerated.lean` — so what this file adds is the identity alone, at
the generality the tag states it, where
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections` of
`UnboundedGlobalSections.lean` has it only for an ideal sheaf with nilpotent local sections.

Every finitely generated `I ⊂ A` is covered: by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIdealSheafGeneratedBy_generatedIdealSheaf` the ideal sheaf
generated by the global sections `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r` is the `I𝒪` of `Ideal.span {a_1, …, a_r}`,
and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy` says
conversely that an `I𝒪` of a finitely generated `I` is of no other shape. The completion on the
module side is the one along `Ideal.span {a_1, …, a_r}`, so the two sides are completed along
matching data.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
